# Byte-exactness pins (2026-07-30): these trees are consumed by hash
# gates (pack manifest verification, battery byte-identical checks,
# replay fixtures) — a fresh clone on Windows must check out the EXACT
# committed bytes, never autocrlf conversions. Without this, a fresh
# checkout CRLF-mangles walkability.json etc. and the world_builder
# hash gate refuses its own repo's pack (flagged at the b65 intake).
# Scripts/docs deliberately keep default handling: no gate hashes
# them, and a repo-wide `* -text` flip would dirty the whole working
# tree (designer decision, not a session's).
assets/** -text
audio/** -text
tileforge_packages/** -text
reports/** -text
tests/replay_fixtures/** -text
*.wsr -text
